## Deploy and watch events

```bash
# One-time: create and fund an identity on testnet
stellar keys generate --global alice --network testnet --fund

stellar contract deploy \
  --wasm target/{% rust_target %}/release/{% crate_name %}.wasm \
  --source alice \
  --network testnet
```

The command prints a contract ID. Invoke it, and each call emits an event:

```bash
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source alice \
  --network testnet \
  -- ping --who alice
```

The emitted events are visible in the transaction result and can be streamed
from an RPC endpoint via `getEvents`.

